This is an automated response to confirm we have received your email.  =20

=20

Please read the section which relates to why you have contacted us. =20

=20

You are bringing or have a complaint with us.=20

=20
If you are bringing a complaint to us and this is your first contact:=20
=20

We are sorry that you have had reason to contact us. The best way to submit=
 your complaint to us is to complete our complaint form. You can complete th=
e complaint form online, or you can get copies of our Parliamentary and Heal=
th forms (including large print format) on our website.=20

=20

If you are unsure if your complaint is ready for us to look at, you can fin=
d out more on our website.=20

=20

If you need a different format such as a different language or Braille, or =
if you need any further support to help you get your complaint to us, you ca=
n call us on 0345 015 4033. We can also provide paper copies of the forms. O=
ur opening hours are Monday to Thursday 9am to 4pm, Friday 8.30am to 12pm=20


2. If you have an existing case with us:=20

=20

Your email will be added to your case and your caseworker will usually be i=
n contact with you =E2=80=82=E2=80=82=E2=80=82=E2=80=82within one month.=20

=20

3. If you are making an FOI request:=20

=20

Please resend your email to informationrights@ombudsman.org.uk. =20



You are contacting us from an organisation or MP's office:=20

=20
If you are providing records or a response to enquiries on a case, your ema=
il will be added to the case and if necessary, the caseworker will be in con=
tact with you. =20
=20
If you have a general query, you will be responded to within one month.=20
=20

If you are emailing about any of the following, please redirect your email:=
=20

Recruitment =E2=80=93 HRSharedservices@ombudsman.org.uk=20
Invoicing =E2=80=93 invoices@ombudsman.org.uk


